			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add codegen emission layer for service schemas and catalog\n\nAdd the code emission layer to Wind's VS Code service codegen pipeline, completing Phase-2 of the system:\n- Codegen.ts: Runnable entry point invoked by prepublishOnly.sh\n- RunCodegen.ts: Orchestrator that walks source tree, extracts decorators, emits schemas\n- EmitServiceSchema.ts: Per-service schema emitter - writes `<Decorator>Upstream.ts` files with typed interface members and source-line back-links\n- EmitServiceCatalog.ts: Catalog emitter - writes ServiceCatalog.ts index of all discovered decorators with metadata\n- index.ts: Public exports for library consumers\n\nThe emission layer takes the ServiceDecoratorRecord extraction results from Phase-1 (added in previous commit) and produces typed TypeScript files under Effect/Generated/ that Wind bridge shapes can import type from. Schema files are idempotent (byte-identical on re-run) with diff-friendly formatting: members sorted by source line, JSDoc preserved verbatim.\n\nRefs: Land/.claude/tauri/Patches/14-StreamingGRPC.md",
			"SHA": "89d68124f9ca9c3443180c16819d407bc3492d4f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:08:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Element): Sync submodule updates with codegen pipeline and production build config\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n\n- Mountain (16bcfef9): Update binary/lib names and Tauri config for production build profile. Rename the Mountain binary and library to include the full production environment profile string (ProductionNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency_22NodeVersion_Bundle_Clean_Compile_ElectronProfile_EsbuildCompiler_Mountain) to distinguish this build variant from development builds. Update tauri.conf.json productName and identifier, and add Binary/node to externalBin for production node path.\n\n- Wind (c4fc5b33): Add VS Code service decorator codegen pipeline and global bridge accessor. Add a new regex-based codegen system that walks the VS Code source tree and extracts `createDecorator(...)` sites with interface members: ExtractDecoratorMatch, ExtractInterfaceMembers, IterateServiceDecorators, SourceTreeWalker. Also adds LandWorkbenchGlobal.ts - typed wrapper around globalThis.__CEL_WIND__ exposing CELWind().RunPromise(...) for Sky consumers.\n\n- Cocoon: Submodule pointer update.\n\nThis synchronization delivers the Wind codegen infrastructure for automated bridge shape generation from upstream VS Code source, while configuring Mountain for production build profile separation.",
			"SHA": "ed7b93f4835433642564a6494d448807fb15e5ff"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:03:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add LandWorkbench composition layer and WorkbenchWorkspace service\n\nSynchronize Wind submodule to deliver a new LandWorkbench composition layer merging all previously-added workbench-tier services (WorkbenchClipboard, Command, Dialog, Host, Keybinding, Lifecycle, Notification, Storage, Theme) plus the new WorkbenchWorkspace service into a single Layer for convenient consumption by Sky.\n\nThe WorkbenchWorkspaceService bridges VS Code's native IWorkspaceService, providing Snapshot (workspace id, folders, configuration), Folders (array of workspace folders), FolderForResource (lookup folder by URI), and OnFolderChange (stream of folder add/remove/change events). The Live implementation reads from globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__.Workspace with proper error handling via WorkbenchWorkspaceProblem ADT.\n\nThe LandWorkbenchLayer uses Layer.mergeAll so a failure in one service doesn't poison others, and LandWorkbenchRuntime provides a lazy singleton ManagedRuntime for efficient per-webview instantiation.\n\nRefs: Land/.claude/tauri/Patches/14-StreamingGRPC.md",
			"SHA": "f26349980f62934c7db60ff00a21b6f635213175"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:01:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Element): Sync submodule updates delivering Workbench service layers\n\nSynchronize multiple Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n- Wind (b91de584): Add WorkbenchClipboard, WorkbenchHost, and WorkbenchKeybinding services. Three new Effect-TS service layers bridging VS Code's native workbench services: WorkbenchClipboardService (read/write text and resources), WorkbenchHostService (reload, restart, close, focus operations), and WorkbenchKeybindingService (keybinding lookup and resolution). Each follows the established Wind pattern with Context.Tag, interface, Live implementation, and Problem ADT.\n- Output, Worker: Submodule pointer updates with internal improvements.\n- Rest, SideCar, Sky: Submodule pointer updates.\n\nThis synchronization delivers the final tier of Wind workbench services, completing the service layer coverage for VS Code integration.",
			"SHA": "77871c6b08f9673b272bb742f3844946326a5b65"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T04:59:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add Workbench* Effect-TS service layers\n\nAdd six new workbench-tier service layers bridging VS Code's native workbench services to Wind's Effect-TS architecture:\n- WorkbenchCommandService: Execute/list/filter commands, stream command execution events\n- WorkbenchDialogService: Confirm dialogs, pick choices, show info/warn/error\n- WorkbenchLifecycleService: Phase tracking (Starting/Ready/Restored/Eventually), shutdown streams\n- WorkbenchNotificationService: Dispatch notifications, stream dispatched events\n- WorkbenchStorageService: Scope-aware (Application/Profile/Workspace) storage with targets\n- WorkbenchThemeService: Get/set color themes, token color queries, theme change streams\n\nEach service provides a typed Effect-TS interface with Live implementation (runtime bridge via globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__) and Problem ADT for error handling, following the established pattern in Wind of exposing Context.Tag, interface, and Layer for dependency injection.\n\nRefs: Land/.claude/tauri/Patches/14-StreamingGRPC.md",
			"SHA": "5ca5ec8c8bb81e041398e9cece2a621d23b4aadb"
		}
